# Target C: exact two-witness source profile for the remaining Profile B

Date: 2026-09-23

Status: rigorous finite strengthening of the sole remaining eight-no-root `k=6,D=-1,p=9` Profile B. The previous quotient-span result leaves witness quotient rank two or three. This note eliminates every source containing three aligned touch-three singleton blocks, then eliminates every source containing two aligned touch-three blocks together with any aligned touch-four singleton block.

Consequently every genuine remaining Profile B source has exactly two aligned touch-three witnesses, no aligned touch-four chosen block, exactly one rank-two singleton block, and six further aligned chosen blocks of touch count at most two. The two witnesses span a two-dimensional subspace of `V/L`; the unique rank-two singleton is dependency-active and supplies the third quotient direction.

Profile B and Target C-II are not yet closed.

Companion exact certificate:

`research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_eight_noroot_k6_dminus1_profile_b_exact_two_witness_profile_2026_09_23.py`

## 1. Inputs already proved

We use the current repository state:

```text
rank(P)=2,
d_1(P)>=4,
d_8=3,
exactly nine chosen singleton changed blocks,
at most one rank-two local-empty singleton block,
at least eight aligned singleton blocks,
at least two dependency-active aligned touch-three witnesses,
witness quotient span H/L has dimension 2 or 3,
if dim(H/L)=2 then exactly one dependency-active non-witness source class exists,
and that class is either aligned touch four or rank two.
```

For an aligned chosen block, all selected source cycles touching that block lie in one four-cycle local direction star. A touch-three aligned block therefore has an exact source touch set equal to a three-subset of one four-star, with the fourth star member absent from the source. Distinct aligned four-stars intersect in at most one no-root cycle.

## 2. Three aligned touch-three blocks are impossible

This exclusion is deliberately stronger than what is needed for quotient rank three. We do not use dependency activity, source-basis kernels, or the minimum-distance condition. We assume only:

```text
8 selected no-root cycles,
rank(P)=2,
virtual canonical deficiency d_8=3,
three distinct aligned chosen root blocks,
each touched by exactly three selected source cycles.
```

### 2.1 Exhaust the root-block geometry

There are `C(35,3)=6545` unordered triples of root triples. Under `S_7` they form exactly ten orbits. Using root-block labels, one representative and orbit size for each orbit is

```text
123,124,125 :  210
123,124,134 :  140
123,124,135 : 1260
123,124,156 : 1260
123,124,345 :  630
123,124,356 : 1260
123,124,567 :  210
123,145,167 :  105
123,145,246 :  840
123,145,267 :  630
```

The orbit sizes sum to `6545`, so the list is exhaustive.

For each representative the certificate enumerates all `3^3` aligned local directions and all choices of the omitted member of each four-star. It keeps exactly those configurations for which each block has exactly three source touches and the union can be extended to an eight-cycle source by adding cycles outside all three full stars.

The last three root-block orbits admit no such eight-cycle source geometry at all.

For the first seven orbits, after quotienting by the stabilizer of the root-block triple, the numbers of distinct eight-cycle source sets are

```text
2259, 261, 1413, 90, 54, 98, 19.
```

### 2.2 Exhaust every rank-two coefficient-plane incidence class

For each source set, let `E_b <= Q^8` be the local empty space at every touched root block. Since `rank(P)=2`, the pattern of incomplete blocks induced by an arbitrary coefficient plane `P` is completely determined by the finite incidences of `P` with the local spaces:

- if `dim E_b=2` and `E_b<=P`, then `P=E_b`;
- two distinct rank-one local lines contained in `P` determine `P` as their span;
- a generic rational plane through one local line realizes exactly that one-line incidence class;
- a generic rational plane avoiding all local lines realizes the empty incidence class.

Thus the same exact incidence enumeration used in the earlier one-touch-three source closures is exhaustive for every rational rank-two `P`.

For each incidence pattern, the certificate forms the virtual-complete root-block set and computes its exact rational dependency rank using the committed `COMPLETE_T` rows. The resulting deficiency histograms, on stabilizer-orbit representatives of the source sets, are:

```text
123,124,125:
  d=4:614, d=5:18790, d=6:94317, d=7:31518,
  d=8:7896, d=9:1677, d=10:287, d=11:33

123,124,134:
  d=5:1579, d=6:13936, d=7:3150, d=8:365, d=9:19

123,124,135:
  d=5:7631, d=6:67639, d=7:20494, d=8:3820,
  d=9:490, d=10:36

123,124,156:
  d=6:6099, d=7:1120, d=8:90

123,124,345:
  d=5:414, d=6:1636, d=7:1303, d=8:333,
  d=9:55, d=10:5

123,124,356:
  d=6:3025, d=7:2797, d=8:1251, d=9:324,
  d=10:56, d=11:6

123,124,567:
  d=6:241, d=7:600, d=8:354, d=9:160,
  d=10:46, d=11:6
```

No incidence pattern in any orbit has `d_8=3`.

Therefore:

```text
A rank-two eight-cycle source of virtual deficiency three
cannot contain three aligned touch-three chosen blocks.      (2.1)
```

This is a strict superset exclusion because no source-basis activity, singleton completeness, coefficient minimum distance, or descendant condition was imposed.

## 3. Two touch-three blocks cannot coexist with an aligned touch-four block

Now assume only that the source contains two aligned touch-three chosen blocks and one aligned touch-four chosen block. Again we do not require any of the three blocks to be dependency-active.

The role-distinguished root-block configurations consist of one touch-four block and an unordered pair of touch-three blocks. There are

```text
35 * C(34,2) = 19635
```

such labeled configurations. Under `S_7` they form exactly seventeen role-preserving orbits; their orbit sizes sum to `19635`.

For each orbit the certificate enumerates all local directions, both omitted touch-three star members, and all source cycles outside the three full stars needed to obtain exactly eight selected cycles.

Only four of the seventeen role orbits admit any source geometry. With the touch-four block written first, representatives are

```text
123 ; 124,125
123 ; 124,134
123 ; 124,135
123 ; 124,145.
```

After stabilizer reduction they give respectively

```text
75, 4, 9, 9
```

eight-cycle source sets.

Running the same exhaustive rank-two coefficient-plane incidence census gives:

```text
123 ; 124,125:
  d=5:371, d=6:4072, d=7:1093, d=8:262,
  d=9:63, d=10:13, d=11:2

123 ; 124,134:
  d=6:286, d=7:51, d=8:4

123 ; 124,135:
  d=6:590, d=7:109, d=8:9

123 ; 124,145:
  d=6:589, d=7:109, d=8:9
```

Again `d_8=3` never occurs. Hence

```text
Once two aligned touch-three chosen blocks are present,
no aligned touch-four chosen block can be present.           (3.1)
```

This is stronger than the preceding source-level result, which excluded only certain dependency-active touch-four profiles.

## 4. Exact remaining chosen-block profile

The preceding quotient-span theorem gave

```text
dim(H/L) in {2,3},
```

where `H` is generated modulo `L` by the dependency-active touch-three witness classes.

If `dim(H/L)=3`, at least three distinct touch-three witnesses are needed. That contradicts (2.1). Therefore

```text
dim(H/L)=2.                                               (4.1)
```

The same theorem then gives exactly one dependency-active source class outside the witness family. It was known to be either aligned touch four or rank two. Equation (3.1) removes the touch-four option. Therefore the complementary active class is rank two.

The earlier two-rank-two closure proves that at most one rank-two singleton block exists at all. Thus there is exactly one.

Equation (2.1) also says there are at most two aligned touch-three chosen blocks. The earlier forcing theorem says there are at least two dependency-active aligned touch-three witnesses. Hence there are exactly two aligned touch-three chosen blocks, and both are the active witnesses.

Finally, Profile B has nine chosen singleton blocks and at most one rank-two block, so exactly eight are aligned. Equation (3.1) rules out aligned touch four, while (2.1) leaves exactly two aligned touch-three blocks. The other six aligned chosen blocks therefore have touch count at most two. The earlier activity lemma says a dependency-active aligned block has touch count three or four, so those six classes lie in `L`.

The remaining chosen-block profile is therefore exactly

```text
2 aligned touch-three blocks, both dependency-active witnesses;
6 aligned blocks of touch count <=2, all dependency-inactive;
1 rank-two singleton block, dependency-active.
```

Modulo `L`, the two touch-three witness classes span a two-dimensional plane and the unique rank-two singleton supplies the third quotient direction.

## 5. Coefficient-line consequence for the unique rank-two singleton

Let `T,U` be the two witness touch triples and let `L_r<=P` be the nonzero coefficient-codeword line supplied by the unique rank-two singleton `r`.

The previously proved line-star bound gives

```text
|supp(L_r) intersect T| <= 1,
|supp(L_r) intersect U| <= 1.
```

Since the two witness stars intersect in at most one cycle,

```text
|T union U| in {5,6}.
```

The coefficient minimum distance gives `wt(L_r)>=4`. Consequently:

- if `T` and `U` are disjoint, so `|T union U|=6`, there are only two source coordinates outside the union and therefore `wt(L_r)=4` exactly; both outside coordinates lie in the support and the support contains exactly two coordinates from `T union U`;
- if `|T union U|=5`, then `wt(L_r)<=5`.

The rank-loss-robust double-witness theorem also applies to the two witnesses. Since they span two quotient dimensions,

```text
d_{T union U} <= 1.                                  (5.1)
```

Thus the final branch is now a single concrete source type with one distinguished low-weight coefficient line and one distinguished five- or six-coordinate puncture of deficiency at most one.

## 6. Remaining bottleneck

Profile B is reduced to the exact profile in Section 4. There are no longer separate witness-rank-three or touch-four-complement branches.

The next target is the unique rank-two complement itself. Combine its coefficient-codeword line with the two exact touch-three stars and the union-puncture bound (5.1). The disjoint-witness case already forces a weight-four support pattern; the one-overlap case forces weight at most five. A finite source-level census can now be restricted to these two patterns rather than the full fixed-nine search.
